To use GitHub with the Eclipse IDE, you will utilize EGit, Eclipse's built-in Git team provider.
Because modern Eclipse installations come with EGit pre-installed, you don't need additional plugins.
However, GitHub requires a Personal Access Token (PAT) or an SSH Key instead of your regular password for security.

Here is how to setup a new GitHub repository and link the repository with the computer.

